<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<display version="2.0.0">
  <name>BLM Calibration</name>
  <macros>
    <P>$(P)</P>
    <CH>$(CH)</CH>
  </macros>
  <width>1090</width>
  <height>660</height>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>Title</name>
    <text>ADC calibration and measurement</text>
    <x>15</x>
    <y>10</y>
    <width>340</width>
    <height>30</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 2" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="18.0">
      </font>
    </font>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>Calibration channel</name>
    <x>340</x>
    <y>10</y>
    <width>738</width>
    <height>87</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 3" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="16.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C0</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>0</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH0</text>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C1</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>1</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH1</text>
      <x>90</x>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C2</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>2</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH2</text>
      <x>180</x>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C3</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>3</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH3</text>
      <x>270</x>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C4</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>4</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH4</text>
      <x>360</x>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>C5</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="open_display">
          <description>Open Display</description>
          <file>blm_calibration.bob</file>
          <macros>
            <P>$(P)</P>
            <CH>5</CH>
          </macros>
          <target>replace</target>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <text>CH5</text>
      <x>450</x>
      <width>85</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Current</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:CUR</pv_name>
      <x>545</x>
      <width>145</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:CUR (ADC_CALI_CUR)

Channel the calibration state machine acts on, CH0..CH5. This is the
calibration target, which is independent of the channel this page is
displaying: the CH buttons above only switch the page, they do not move the
target. Measure / Calibrate, Save, Reload and Reset all apply to the target
selected here, so check it before pressing Measure / Calibrate.

Takes effect as soon as you pick an entry. The enum restricts the value to
0..5; anything larger would index past the channel array in
the rawdata acquisition task.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>CH0</item>
        <item>CH1</item>
        <item>CH2</item>
        <item>CH3</item>
        <item>CH4</item>
        <item>CH5</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>CurrentLabel</name>
      <text>Calibration target</text>
      <x>545</x>
      <y>32</y>
      <width>145</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
  </widget>
  <widget type="embedded" version="2.0.0">
    <name>Measure</name>
    <macros>
      <P>$(P)</P>
      <CH>$(CH)</CH>
    </macros>
    <file>blm_measure.bob</file>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>97</y>
    <width>638</width>
    <height>190</height>
    <resize>true</resize>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>Action</name>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>348</y>
    <width>1066</width>
    <height>172</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 3" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="16.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Title</name>
      <text>Calibration action</text>
      <width>250</width>
      <height>24</height>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>MeasureCount</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:MEASURE_COUNT</pv_name>
      <x>39</x>
      <y>80</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>30</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:MEASURE_COUNT (ADC_CALI_MEASURE_COUNT)

Number of rawdata frames collected by Measure. Each top/bottom window rejects
outliers using a 5x MAD rule, then the per-frame robust results are combined by
median to calculate editable candidates. Range 1..100; default 5. Normal
rawdata and MEAS values still use the latest frame.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>MeasureCountLabel</name>
      <text>Measure samples</text>
      <x>39</x>
      <y>110</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Select</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:SEL</pv_name>
      <x>39</x>
      <y>24</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:SEL (ADC_CALI_SEL)

Selects which quantity the calibration run solves for:
  Offset B - measure the baseline over the bottom window and shift it onto
             Calibration base, updating the offset coefficients.
  Gain K   - measure the span and scale it so the signal matches the expected
             amplitude, updating the gain coefficients.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>Offset B</item>
        <item>Gain K</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="combo" version="2.0.0">
      <name>BOrK</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:B_OR_K</pv_name>
      <x>274</x>
      <y>24</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:B_OR_K (ADC_CALI_B_OR_K)

Selects which coefficient set the calibration run writes to:
  Factory B - the first stage coefficients (K0, B0) that come from the factory
              characterization of the board.
  Field K   - the second stage coefficients (K1, B1) that are adjusted in the
              field during maintenance.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
      <items>
        <item>Factory</item>
        <item>Field</item>
      </items>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Measure</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Acquire one calibration snapshot</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:MEASURE</pv_name>
      <text>Measure</text>
      <x>509</x>
      <y>24</y>
      <width>110</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Acquires the configured number of fresh rawdata frames. Each top/bottom window
uses 5x MAD outlier rejection, and the per-frame robust results are combined
by median for candidate calculation. The latest frame remains the normal
waveform/measurement display; active coefficients are unchanged.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Apply</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Apply the editable candidate coefficients</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:APPLY</pv_name>
      <text>Apply</text>
      <x>629</x>
      <y>24</y>
      <width>110</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Submits the complete editable candidate coefficient set for the selected
channel. Requires a successful Measure. Manual candidate edits do not change
the waveform until Apply; Save is required for file persistence.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
      <name>State</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:STATE</pv_name>
      <x>744</x>
      <y>24</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:STATE (ADC_CALI_STATE)

State: Idle, Measuring, Measured, Applying, Applied, or Error. Apply is valid
only in Measured state.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>SelectLabel</name>
      <text>Calibration mode</text>
      <x>39</x>
      <y>58</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>BOrKLabel</name>
      <text>Coefficient set</text>
      <x>274</x>
      <y>58</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>TriggerLabel</name>
      <text>Start Calibration</text>
      <x>509</x>
      <y>58</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>StatusLabel</name>
      <text>State</text>
      <x>744</x>
      <y>58</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textupdate" version="2.0.0">
      <name>Error</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:ERROR</pv_name>
      <x>274</x>
      <y>80</y>
      <width>695</width>
      <height>28</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <vertical_alignment>1</vertical_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CALI:ERROR (ADC_CALI_ERROR)

Last calibration error. Empty means no error.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>ErrorLabel</name>
      <text>Error Message</text>
      <x>509</x>
      <y>108</y>
      <width>225</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>ADC coefficient files</name>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>275</y>
    <width>619</width>
    <height>73</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 3" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="16.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Save</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Save coefficients to file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:SAVE</pv_name>
      <text>Save</text>
      <x>17</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>160</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Writes the coefficients of all six channels currently held by the driver to
the calibration coefficient file, so they survive an IOC restart. Run this
after a successful calibration.</tooltip>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Reload</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Reload coefficients from file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:RLD</pv_name>
      <text>Reload</text>
      <x>216</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>160</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Discards the coefficients in the driver and reads them back from the
calibration coefficient file. Use this to undo an unsaved calibration run.</tooltip>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>Reset</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Reset coefficients to defaults</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):CALI:RST</pv_name>
      <text>Reset</text>
      <x>415</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>160</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Resets the coefficients of the calibration target channel selected above
($(P):CALI:CUR) to the identity calibration K0=1, B0=0, K1=1, B1=0. The file
on disk is not touched until you press Save.</tooltip>
    </widget>
  </widget>
  <widget type="embedded" version="2.0.0">
    <name>Coefficients</name>
    <macros>
      <P>$(P)</P>
      <CH>$(CH)</CH>
    </macros>
    <file>blm_calibration_coefficients.bob</file>
    <x>650</x>
    <y>97</y>
    <width>447</width>
    <height>250</height>
  </widget>
  <widget type="group" version="3.0.0">
    <name>Setpoint and dose files</name>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>530</y>
    <width>1069</width>
    <height>100</height>
    <font>
      <font name="Header 3" family="Liberation Sans" style="BOLD" size="16.0">
      </font>
    </font>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DoseSave</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Save dose K/B to file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):DOSE_CALI:SAVE</pv_name>
      <text>Save dose K/B</text>
      <x>264</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>112</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Writes the dose coefficients (K, B) of all six channels currently held by the
driver to ${BLMCALIB}/dose_calib_params.txt, so they survive an IOC restart.
Run this after editing DOSE_CALI_K / DOSE_CALI_B on the channel detail
page.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DoseReload</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Reload dose K/B from file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):DOSE_CALI:RLD</pv_name>
      <text>Reload dose K/B</text>
      <x>387</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>112</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Discards the dose coefficients in the driver, reads them back from
${BLMCALIB}/dose_calib_params.txt and re-publishes every channel's DOSE from
its cached 100 ms fiber count. Use this to undo an unsaved dose
calibration.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DoseCaliB</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DOSE_CALI_B</pv_name>
      <x>130</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>34</height>
      <format>3</format>
      <precision>4</precision>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DOSE_CALI_B (DOSE_CALI_CH$(CH)_B)

Offset B (uSv/h) of the dose calibration of channel $(CH), added after the
K*cnt term: it is the dose shown when the fiber count is zero (the electronic
baseline). Default 0; any finite value is accepted and re-publishes the dose
immediately. Persist with $(P):DOSE_CALI:SAVE.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DoseCaliK</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DOSE_CALI_K</pv_name>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>34</height>
      <format>3</format>
      <precision>4</precision>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DOSE_CALI_K (DOSE_CALI_CH$(CH)_K)

Slope K (uSv/h per fiber count) of the dose calibration of channel $(CH):
DOSE = K * FBR_CNT_100MS + B. A new K re-publishes the dose immediately from
the cached count. Default 1; must be finite and non-zero - 0 is rejected and
the previous value retained. Persist with $(P):DOSE_CALI:SAVE.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>DoseCaliKLabel</name>
      <text>Dose K</text>
      <y>35</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>DoseCaliBLabel</name>
      <text>Dose B</text>
      <x>130</x>
      <y>35</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DACCaliK</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_CALI_K</pv_name>
      <x>509</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>34</height>
      <format>3</format>
      <precision>4</precision>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_CALI_K (DAC_CALI_CH$(CH)_K)

Slope K of the DAC setpoint calibration of channel $(CH). The driver sends
K*x + B (mV) to the DAC80508 for the DAC_REF_SP value x, so a new K
re-applies the current setpoint immediately. Default 1; must be finite and
non-zero - 0 is rejected and the previous value is retained. Persist with
$(P):DAC_CALI:SAVE, restore with $(P):DAC_CALI:RLD.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>DACCaliKLabel</name>
      <text>DAC K</text>
      <x>509</x>
      <y>38</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="textentry" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DACCaliB</name>
      <pv_name>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_CALI_B</pv_name>
      <x>640</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>34</height>
      <format>3</format>
      <precision>4</precision>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
      <tooltip>$(P):CH$(CH):DAC_CALI_B (DAC_CALI_CH$(CH)_B)

Offset B (mV) of the DAC setpoint calibration of channel $(CH), added after
the K*x term. Default 0; any finite value is accepted, but the transformed
K*x + B still has to land inside 0 to 2500 mV or the setpoint is refused.
Persist with $(P):DAC_CALI:SAVE, restore with $(P):DAC_CALI:RLD.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
      <name>DACCaliBLabel</name>
      <text>DAC B</text>
      <x>647</x>
      <y>38</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>22</height>
      <horizontal_alignment>1</horizontal_alignment>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DacSave</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Save DAC K/B to file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):DAC_CALI:SAVE</pv_name>
      <text>Save DAC K/B</text>
      <x>770</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Writes the DAC setpoint coefficients (K, B) of all six channels currently
held by the driver to ${BLMCALIB}/dac_calib_params.txt, so they survive an
IOC restart. Run this after editing DAC_CALI_K / DAC_CALI_B on the channel
detail page.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
    <widget type="action_button" version="3.0.0">
      <name>DacReload</name>
      <actions>
        <action type="write_pv">
          <description>Reload DAC K/B from file</description>
          <pv_name>$(pv_name)</pv_name>
          <value>1</value>
        </action>
      </actions>
      <pv_name>$(P):DAC_CALI:RLD</pv_name>
      <text>Reload DAC K/B</text>
      <x>900</x>
      <y>1</y>
      <width>120</width>
      <height>32</height>
      <tooltip>$(actions)

Discards the DAC setpoint coefficients in the driver, reads them back from
${BLMCALIB}/dac_calib_params.txt and re-applies them by re-sending every
channel's current DAC_REF_SP through K*x + B. Use this to undo an unsaved
DAC calibration.</tooltip>
      <border_alarm_sensitive>false</border_alarm_sensitive>
    </widget>
  </widget>
  <widget type="label" version="2.0.0">
    <name>Copyright</name>
    <text>(C) 2026 IMPCAS | Beam Feedback Group | Ren Fei</text>
    <x>12</x>
    <y>640</y>
    <width>600</width>
    <height>18</height>
    <foreground_color>
      <color red="100" green="100" blue="100">
      </color>
    </foreground_color>
  </widget>
</display>
